# Formatting and Linting

This project formats with Prettier (`.prettierrc`) and lints with ESLint (`.eslintrc.json`). Editor format-on-save and ESLint diagnostics are configured in `.vscode/settings.json`, which Cursor reads directly. A husky pre-commit hook runs `lint-staged` (eslint --fix + prettier) on staged files.

When writing or editing code, match the Prettier config:

- No semicolons
- Single quotes
- 2-space indentation, no tabs
- 100 character print width
- Trailing commas (ES5 positions: arrays, objects — not function args)
- Arrow function parens omitted for single params (`x => x`)
- LF line endings

Follow the ESLint rules: `const` over `let` where possible, never `var`, `===` over `==` (except `== null`), nullish coalescing (`??`) and optional chaining (`?.`) preferred, object shorthand, arrow callbacks, explicit return types on functions (warn), no `console.log` in `src/` (`console.warn`/`console.error` allowed; any console allowed in `tools/`).

Useful commands:

- `npm run format` — format every file in the repo
- `npm run format:file -- path/to/file.ts` — format one file
- `npm run lint:fix` — auto-fix ESLint issues
